{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git status --porcelain=v1; git rev-parse HEAD; rg -n 'module|scope|case|carry' pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md | tail -12\"","aggregated_output":"2f2c1ab0fe9eaaff5d32a7803e97c9c7989542b6\n7:`enforced` case fails the build when the shortcut works again; a `known-gap`\n8:case fails the build when the gap closes, so it cannot close or reopen\n9:silently; a `planned` case belongs to a spec not yet delivered and gains code\n10:before that spec closes; a `delegated` case is enforced by a test in another\n31:| `ready-from-absent-blockers` | enforced | Absence of a known blocker is presented as proven independence | pose-phase-scoped-readiness |\n36:| `unpinned-premise-trigger-reads-current` | enforced | A premise trigger without a pin can never go stale and nothing says so | pose-assumption-validity-scope |\n37:| `calendar-ttl-as-premise-trigger` | enforced | An arbitrary expiry date is accepted as the material trigger of a premise | pose-assumption-validity-scope |\n40:| `imported-fragment-completes-a-replaced-command` | known-gap | A usage or error string assembles a removed command from a constant of another package of the module, which the active-document check reads as a gap; review of assembled messages is the defence | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n47:| `run-pattern-names-no-test` | delegated | A validation check's `-run` alternative names a test that no longer exists, or never did, and the check passes on Go's exit 0 — through `-run=`, a build-excluded or ignored file, a vendored or nested-module declaration, a benchmark or a name Go does not run (`cli/validation_matrix_patterns_test.go:TestDeadRunPatternGuardFollowsGoSelection`, `cli/validation_matrix_patterns_test.go:TestValidationMatrixRunPatternsNameExistingTests`); a non-plain pattern passes only when listed with its reason | pose-validation-matrix-dead-test-patterns |\n54:| `witness-bundle-filter-hides-loss` | delegated | Editing a witness bundle makes scoped readers skip its corruption | pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"The build, vet, targeted regressions, and targeted race tests pass. `artifact-check --strict` also exits successfully, though it reports repository-wide orphan warnings and resolves a wider trailer range than the sealed subject, as the brief anticipated. I’m waiting for the two strict validation runs and the broader package tests.\n"}}
