{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"web_search","id":"exec-5ea1501a-73e1-46a5-bfbd-51a63d9e6d85","query":"site.kernel.org ext4 case insensitive per-directory +F casefold","action":{"type":"search","query":"site.kernel.org ext4 case insensitive per-directory +F casefold"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.kernel.org","ref_id":"turn1search0","snippet":"The case-insensitive file name lookup feature is supported on a per-directory basis, allowing the user to mix case-insensitive and case-sensitive directories in the same filesystem.","title":"ext4 General Information — The Linux Kernel documentation","url":"https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/ext4.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"origin.kernel.org","ref_id":"turn1search1","snippet":"The case-insensitive file name lookup feature is supported on a per-directory basis, allowing the user to mix case-insensitive and case-sensitive directories in the same filesystem.","title":"ext4 General Information — The Linux Kernel documentation","url":"https://origin.kernel.org/doc/html/v5.19/admin-guide/ext4.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"lists.openwall.net","ref_id":"turn1search2","snippet":"linux-ext4@...r.kernel.org, ... Subject: [PATCH v6 07/16] ext4: Report case sensitivity in fileattr_get ... Case sensitivity is a per-directory setting in ext4. ... inode is a","title":"linux-ext4 - [PATCH v6 07/16] ext4: Report case sensitivity in fileattr_get","url":"https://lists.openwall.net/linux-ext4/2026/01/20/37"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"lists.openwall.net","ref_id":"turn1search3","snippet":"Cc: linux-fsdevel@...r.kernel.org, linux-ext4@...r.kernel.org, ... Subject: [PATCH v10 08/17] ext4: Report case sensitivity in fileattr_get ... Case sensitivity is a per-directory setting in ext4. ...","title":"linux-ext4 - [PATCH v10 08/17] ext4: Report case sensitivity in fileattr_get","url":"https://lists.openwall.net/linux-ext4/2026/04/23/22"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"linux.googlesource.com","ref_id":"turn1search4","snippet":"| case-insensitive file name lookups ... | per-directory basis, allowing the user to mix case-insensitive and ... | flipping the +F inode attribute of an","title":"Documentation/admin-guide/ext4.rst - linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux - Git at Google","url":"https://linux.googlesource.com/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux/%2B/79ba234b396b0fdcb3a82dd8aa872348f4069aae/Documentation/admin-guide/ext4.rst"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"kernel.googlesource.com","ref_id":"turn1search5","snippet":"| casefold feature, which stores the filesystem-wide encoding ... | followed by a byte per byte comparison. ... | impact on where the directory entry","title":"Documentation/admin-guide/ext4.rst - pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git - Git at Google","url":"https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/%2B/26b77009ee74f6122a067a4f9926ff6e09fffb94/Documentation/admin-guide/ext4.rst"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.kernel.org","ref_id":"turn1search6","snippet":"bcachefs has support for case-insensitive file and directory lookups using the regular chattr +F (S_CASEFOLD, FS_CASEFOLD_FL) casefolding attributes. ... Casefolding support requires a kernel with","title":"1. Casefolding — The Linux Kernel documentation","url":"https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/next/filesystems/bcachefs/casefolding.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"kernel.googlesource.com","ref_id":"turn1search7","snippet":"| * efficient new ordered mode in JBD2 and ext4 (avoid using buffer head to force ... | * Case-insensitive file name lookups ... |","title":"Documentation/admin-guide/ext4.rst - pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git - Git at Google","url":"https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/%2B/85cdaca6970028bf6f544c355c90035586836ddf/Documentation/admin-guide/ext4.rst"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"lists.openwall.net","ref_id":"turn1search8","snippet":"Cc: linux-ext4@...r.kernel.org, sfrench@...ba.org, ... index e506d3dae510..4e08d0309f1e 100644 ... +* Case insensitive file name lookups ... +because it is what defines the casefold operation. ... +gr","title":"linux-ext4 - [PATCH RFC v6 11/11] docs: ext4.rst: Document encoding and case-insensitive","url":"https://lists.openwall.net/linux-ext4/2019/03/18/20"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"lists.openwall.net","ref_id":"turn1search9","snippet":"Cc: linux-ext4@...r.kernel.org, ... A filesystem that has the fname_encoding feature set is able to ... per byte match with the disk name, but is an","title":"linux-ext4 - [PATCH v7 09/10] ext4: Support case-insensitive file name lookups","url":"https://lists.openwall.net/linux-ext4/2019/04/13/16"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.usenix.org","ref_id":"turn1search12","snippet":"In 2019, Linux kernel version 5.2 added support for per-directory case-insensitivity to ext4 [12, 34]. Later in 2019, similar support was added to the Flash-Friendly","title":"Researchers have long been aware of hazards that may occur during file system name resolution [3, 4], particularly that programmers must validate safe use of symbolic links and check for \"squatted\" files when creating a new files. Many defenses have been proposed [7–9, 30, 40–42, 50–52, 55]. However, to the best of our knowledge, ours is the first work studying how case interplays cause name collisions that lead to incorrect, and in some cases, vulnerable behaviors. We show that utilities and applications currently do not recognize unsafe use of case-insensitive file systems, leading to these problems. This paper demonstrates the potential implications of the name collision problem, focusing on Linux and its supported file systems, thereby motivating both more and broader (e.g., other OS-FS combination) investigations. We identify potential gaps in the existing contract between the applications and the underlying file system that results in unsafe behaviors (see §8). We make the following contributions:","url":"https://www.usenix.org/system/files/fast23_full_proceedings.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"lists.openwall.net","ref_id":"turn1search10","snippet":"Cc: linux-ext4@...r.kernel.org, kernel@...labora.com, ... which states that the directory requires case-insensitive searches. ... +#define EXT4_CASEFOLD_FL 0x00100000 /* Casefolded file */ ... index 7","title":"linux-ext4 - [PATCH v2 24/25] ext4: Implement EXT4_CASEFOLD_FL flag","url":"https://lists.openwall.net/linux-ext4/2018/08/15/28"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"mirrors.hust.edu.cn","ref_id":"turn1search11","snippet":"+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/ext4.rst@@ -91,10 +91,48 @@ Currently Available * large block (up to pagesize) support * efficient new ordered mode in JBD2 and ext4 (avoid using","title":"docs: ext4.rst: document case-insensitive directories - linux.git - Linux kernel mainline source","url":"https://mirrors.hust.edu.cn/git/linux.git/commit/Documentation/admin-guide/ext4.rst?id=0a790fe4389d88253563c5e22bea47e6d357b525"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.igalia.com","ref_id":"turn1search13","snippet":"User needs to explicitly ask to a directory to ... Currently supported by ext4, f2fs, tmpfs and overlayfs ... work with casefold mount points Implementing","title":"Implementing case-insensitive ﬁle","url":"https://www.igalia.com/downloads/slides/AndreAlmeida-ImplementingCaseInsensitiveFileSystemsInTheLinuxKernel.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"blog.foool.net","ref_id":"turn1search14","snippet":"The case-insensitive file name lookup feature is supported on a per-directory basis, allowing the user to mix case-insensitive and case-sensitive directories in the same filesystem.","title":"Linux Admin-guide Documentation","url":"https://blog.foool.net/wp-content/uploads/linuxdocs/admin-guide.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.mywebuniversity.com","ref_id":"turn1search15","snippet":"http://ext4.wiki.kernel.org/index.php/Bigalloc for details. ... This ext4 feature provides file system level character encoding support for direc? tories with the casefold (+F) flag enabled. ... more","title":"Rocky Enterprise Linux 9.2 Manual Pages on command 'ext2.5'","url":"https://www.mywebuniversity.com/Man_PDF/ext2.5.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.mywebuniversity.com","ref_id":"turn1search16","snippet":"A directory with the ’F’ attribute set indicates that all the path lookups inside that directory are made in a case-insensitive fashion. This attribute can","title":"CHATTR(1)　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　 General Commands Manual　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　 CHATTR(1)","url":"https://www.mywebuniversity.com/man2pdf/chattr.1.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.mywebuniversity.com","ref_id":"turn1search17","snippet":"file systems with this ext4 feature enabled. ... Please see the web page http://ext4.wiki.kernel.org/in? ... support for directories with the casefold (+F) flag enabled.","title":"Rocky Enterprise Linux 9.2 Manual Pages on command 'ext4.5'","url":"https://www.mywebuniversity.com/Rocky_92/Man_PDF/ext4.5.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.youtube.com","ref_id":"turn1youtube18","snippet":"# Implementing Case-insensitive File Systems in the Linux Kernel - André Almeida, Igalia ... After ext4, several other file systems have implemented this feature, such","title":"Implementing Case-insensitive File Systems in the Linux Kernel - André Almeida, Igalia - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N01lJ0iV4ss"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.youtube.com","ref_id":"turn1youtube19","snippet":"Historically, file and directory names have always been treated as opaque byte sequences by Unix kernels, in opposition to what was always done in Windows","title":"Ext4: A Case-insensitive Linux Filesystem - Gabriel Krisman Bertazi, Collabora - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVlEZKiMGJU"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.reddit.com","ref_id":"turn1reddit20","snippet":"> A directory with the 'F' attribute set indicates that all the path lookups inside that directory are made in a case-insensitive fashion. This attribute","title":"ext4 case insensivity","url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/linuxquestions/comments/hp85ll"}]}}
