{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"The broader CLI package tests pass. I’m treating the enclosing-directory case as a dependency-declaration assumption under R6, rather than a new blocker. A stronger case-related gap remains: the probe checks only the root `.git` entry, but Linux supports case-folding per directory. A case-sensitive root can therefore hide case aliases in module inputs, leaving R6-N18 partially fixed.\n"}}
