{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat scripts/test-engine-go.sh; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json'))\nfor c in m.get('moduleOverrides',{}).get('pose-mcp',{}).get('checks',[]):\n if c.get('name') in ['test','cli-test-wall-time-integration']:\n  print(c)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" && pwd -P)\"\ncd \"$ROOT/pose-mcp\"\nexport LC_ALL=C\n\nmode=\"${1:-all}\"\nif [ \"$#\" -gt 1 ]; then\n  mode=invalid\nfi\ncase \"$mode\" in\n  all|other|pose-0|pose-1|inventory) ;;\n  *) printf '%s\\n' 'usage: test-engine-go.sh [all|other|pose-0|pose-1|inventory]' >&2; exit 2 ;;\nesac\n\nrun_other_packages() {\n  local heavy listed package\n  local -a other=()\n  heavy=\"$(go list ./internal/pose)\"\n  listed=\"$(go list ./...)\"\n  while IFS= read -r package; do\n    if [ \"$package\" != \"$heavy\" ]; then\n      other+=(\"$package\")\n    fi\n  done <<< \"$listed\"\n  if [ \"${#other[@]}\" -eq 0 ] || [ \"${#other[@]}\" -eq \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$listed\" | wc -l)\" ]; then\n    printf '%s\\n' 'test-engine-go: the Go package inventory did not contain the expected package split' >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  go test -timeout 10m -count=1 \"${other[@]}\"\n}\n\nlist_names() {\n  go test -list \"$1\" ./internal/pose | sed -n -E '/^(Test|Fuzz|Example)[^[:space:]]*$/p' | sort\n}\n\nprepare_pose_shards() {\n  local all selected0 selected1 combined test_name\n  local i=0\n  local -a first=() second=()\n  all=\"$(list_names '^(Test|Fuzz|Example)')\"\n  while IFS= read -r test_name; do\n    if [ \"$((i % 2))\" -eq 0 ]; then\n      first+=(\"$test_name\")\n    else\n      second+=(\"$test_name\")\n    fi\n    i=$((i + 1))\n  done <<< \"$all\"\n  if [ -z \"$all\" ] || [ \"${#second[@]}\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    printf '%s\\n' 'test-engine-go: expected two nonempty Go test shards' >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  pose_pattern_0=\"^($(IFS='|'; printf '%s' \"${first[*]}\"))$\"\n  pose_pattern_1=\"^($(IFS='|'; printf '%s' \"${second[*]}\"))$\"\n  selected0=\"$(list_names \"$pose_pattern_0\")\"\n  selected1=\"$(list_names \"$pose_pattern_1\")\"\n  combined=\"$(printf '%s\\n%s\\n' \"$selected0\" \"$selected1\" | sort)\"\n  if [ \"$combined\" != \"$all\" ]; then\n    printf '%s\\n' 'test-engine-go: the Go-selected shards overlap or omit a test' >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  printf 'internal/pose inventory: %d + %d = %d tests, fuzz targets and examples\\n'     \"${#first[@]}\" \"${#second[@]}\" \"$i\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$mode\" = other ]; then\n  run_other_packages\n  exit 0\nfi\n\nprepare_pose_shards\ncase \"$mode\" in\n  all)\n    run_other_packages\n    go test -timeout 10m -count=1 -run \"$pose_pattern_0\" ./internal/pose\n    go test -timeout 10m -count=1 -run \"$pose_pattern_1\" ./internal/pose\n    ;;\n  pose-0) go test -timeout 10m -count=1 -run \"$pose_pattern_0\" ./internal/pose ;;\n  pose-1) go test -timeout 10m -count=1 -run \"$pose_pattern_1\" ./internal/pose ;;\n  inventory) ;;\nesac\n{'name': 'test', 'program': 'bash', 'args': ['../scripts/test-engine-go.sh'], 'severity': 'required', 'evidenceClass': 'unit', 'timeoutSeconds': 1800}\n{'name': 'cli-test-wall-time-integration', 'program': 'go', 'args': ['test', './internal/cli', '-run', 'TestDelegateToolsOverMCPHoldAgainstTheFirstReview|TestDelegateToolsOverMCPMatchTheCLI|TestADetachedRun|TestDelegateDetachAndWait|TestTheWaitAcknowledgementNeverTouchesAnExistingEntry|TestReviewDispatchJudgesTheRunNotItsLeftovers|TestDelegateWatchFollowsLive|TestPreviewCarriesVerboseAndLsReadsLiveProgress', '-count=1'], 'severity': 'required', 'evidenceClass': 'integration'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nPrevious findings are accounted for below: R5-N16, R6-N17 and R6-N18 remain partial; R6-N19 is fixed.\n\nFour high-severity blockers remain:\n\n- **R7-N20:** The symlink scan skips submodule contents, allowing declared dependency aliases inside gitlinks to retain stale passes. Gitlinks reference separate repositories’ commits. [Git documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/gitsubmodules.html)\n- **R7-N21:** `material_clean` ignores untracked inputs created during validation.\n- **R7-N22:** The case-sensitivity probe examines only the root directory. Linux permits case-sensitive and case-folded directories within one filesystem. [Kernel documentation](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/ext4.html)\n- **R7-N23:** Git configuration can hide changed gitlinks. I reproduced this with the existing regression test under `diff.ignoreSubmodules=all`: validation selected zero modules and reported SUCCESS. [Git documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-diff)\n\nTargeted tests, race tests, build and vet passed. Both strict validation commands exited 1; repository-wide validation reported 235/236 passing. The broader `internal/pose` test run timed out. The sealed canonical results remain historical green evidence, not a fresh local pass. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N16\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink passes in the targeted run. validate_carry.go:272-319 now rejects relevant symlinks tracked in the superproject, but its ls-tree scan does not inspect submodule trees; R7-N20 covers the remaining declared-dependency alias gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R6-N17\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule passes in the targeted run and covers the original missing-leaf scenario. The guard reads tracked symlink entries independently of leaf existence, but symlinks tracked inside gitlinks remain invisible at validate_carry.go:273; see R7-N20.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R6-N18\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem passes for the modeled uniform filesystem. validate_carry.go:324-330 probes only root/.git and root/.GIT. This does not establish case sensitivity in module or dependency directories; ext4 supports per-directory case folding. See R7-N22.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R6-N19\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs passes in the targeted run. validate_carry.go rejects duplicate effective matrix IDs and duplicate base IDs before constructing the base map; duplicateCheckID checks defaults together with appended overrides.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R7-N20\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 273,\n      \"summary\": \"The alias scan runs ls-tree only on the superproject, so it sees gitlinks but not symlinks tracked inside them. For a discovered submodule b, let b/link point to ../a and declare b dependsOn=['b/link/input']. Changing a/input leaves the submodule clean and selects a, while lexical dependency matching misses b/link/input. Neither aliasedModule nor aliasingSymlink detects this alias, so b can carry a stale pass. This violates R2 and D1 even with an explicit dependency declaration. Inspect relevant submodule trees and aliases, or conservatively refuse carry when their safety cannot be established. Established by source analysis, not a new writable fixture.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R7-N21\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1425,\n      \"summary\": \"The new material_clean flag uses materialTrackedUnchanged at the end of the run. That helper explicitly passes --untracked-files=no at line 1730. A run can start clean, observe an untracked source/input file created while checks are running, and finish with material_clean=true although that input is absent from its recorded commit. Removing the untracked input afterward and committing only the canonical record lets carry reuse the resulting pass over the unchanged, failing committed material. R2 requires the working copy to match the recorded head at both endpoints. Include non-ignored material untracked inputs in the end check. The targeted MaterialTrackedUnchanged test confirms the helper's deliberate omission; the complete carry sequence was established by source analysis.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R7-N22\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 329,\n      \"summary\": \"Checking whether root/.GIT aliases root/.git proves only the root directory's lookup behavior. On ext4, a case-sensitive root may contain a case-folded directory a. With tracked a/input and b declaring dependsOn=['a/INPUT'], b can correctly read that declared physical input while changed-scope comparison matches neither spelling. Editing a/input selects a but leaves b carried: module directories remain distinct, no symlink exists, and the root probe accepts the filesystem. This leaves R6-N18 partial and violates R2/D1. Establish case safety for relevant input directories and dependency spellings, or refuse ambiguous cases. Platform behavior is verified by official kernel documentation; this filesystem scenario was not locally mounted or reproduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R7-N23\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 88,\n      \"summary\": \"The changed-path diff inherits diff.ignoreSubmodules and submodule ignore configuration because it does not force --ignore-submodules=none. Setting diff.ignoreSubmodules=all hides a committed gitlink update, so modules beneath that path and consumers declaring dependencies beneath it are not selected. I reproduced this without repository edits: go test ./internal/cli/ -run '^TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents$' -count=1 -exec 'env GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1 GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=diff.ignoreSubmodules GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=all' fails with '0 changed file(s), 0/2 module(s) selected' and validation reports SUCCESS. Force complete gitlink visibility in the authoritative diff. This affects both --changed-from and --carry and violates R3, R6 and D1.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the full listed subject against R1-R10 and D1-D3, including CLI restrictions, base comparability, engine stamping, pinned heads, clean-material handling, administrative exclusions, outcome/count preservation, chained origins, delivery parsing, docs/help and scaffold parity. Swept gitlinks/submodules, symlinks, case aliases, quoted names, renames, deleted and nested dependencies, manifestless moduleOverrides, effective stack/check changes, criticality widening, transitive selection, cancellation and canonical publication. Nested cross-module reads remain dependent on declared edges under R6; I did not report the enclosing-directory case as an additional blocker. Existing publication uses the governance guard and atomic authoritative publication. Targeted carry/selection/identity/material/publication tests and targeted race tests passed; build and vet passed. The broader CLI package passed in 312 seconds, while internal/pose hit the ten-minute timeout. Both strict validation invocations exited 1; the global run reported 235/236 passing. The configured-gitlink counterexample failed independently as described in R7-N23. Persisting assessments were not run because scratch creation was denied by the read-only filesystem. No repository edits or attestation were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R7-N22\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the assumptions of complete changed-path enumeration, lexical dependency identity, clean committed inputs and complete instance declarations. Uniform case sensitivity is not established by the root probe. Explicit dependency declarations remain an instance responsibility under R6/D3.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R7-N21\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Targeted race and publication tests pass, but concurrent creation of untracked material during a run can escape the new end-of-run cleanliness assertion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected additive validation fields, retained schema version, old-record fallback and CLI restrictions. No incompatible CLI, MCP or file-field removal was found.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Targeted tests exercised incompatible flags, unusable bases, malformed metadata, duplicate IDs and fallback reasons. Revision arguments are confined before Git calls.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R7-N20\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Delivery parsing preserves carried origin heads, but input attribution across the superproject/submodule boundary remains unsound.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected carry reasons, selected-module explanations, retained bounded check output, counts and origin fields. Covered refusal paths return actionable context without adding sensitive environment output.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"New fields and the flag are additive. Older records retain their reader behavior and cannot become eligible carry bases without the required new provenance fields.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R7-N23\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The configured-gitlink regression independently demonstrates an incomplete changed set and a successful result with no selected modules. R7-N20 through R7-N22 identify additional safety gaps.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R7-N22\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 addresses repeated full validation by retaining original observations and rebinding only unchanged inputs. D2 and D3 limit reuse through whole-matrix/engine comparison and explicit declarations. The alias and changed-set counterexamples invalidate D1's safety premise; retaining carried_from alone does not repair an incorrect current material binding.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-a9e60b2a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The added ADR records carrying unchanged observations with their true origins, the declaration boundary and the fallback trade-off that D1 relies on.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared English and pt-BR manuals, help and embedded scaffold updates with the intended R1-R10 contract. Carry restrictions, fields, fallback behavior and selfContained responsibility are documented. The English scaffold difference is the existing instance-only contributor section.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined base refusal explanations, explain output, counts, origin metadata and publication errors. The implemented refusal paths explain how to obtain a comparable canonical run; the open findings concern missed invalidation rather than an absence of diagnostics on detected failures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R7-N21\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R2's end-of-run clean-material guarantee is not met. R7-N20, R7-N22 and R7-N23 also defeat R2/R3/R6 and D1 despite passing ordinary regression fixtures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7af84b6b13c1a047\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the declared artifacts and subject diff with the spec. The implementation remains within validation selection/results, delivery consumption, help, documentation and the required ADR. Artifact-check exited 0, while resolving the wider trailer range described in the brief.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R7-N20\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision confinement and raw-history protections are retained, and no new dependencies or secrets were found in the changed code. However, the submodule alias boundary can authorize stale evidence as current material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing module selection with additive provenance and conservative fallback is smaller than per-check arbitrary-input caching and addresses the stated cost. It avoids speculative cache machinery. The choice remains appropriate only while input identity and changed-set completeness can be established; otherwise carry must refuse, including the open counterexamples.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed and exited 0. It reported repository-wide orphan warnings and resolved a wider trailer range than the sealed subject; that limitation was not treated as proof of a new subject defect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7af84b6b13c1a047\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose assess design --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --json. Its input digest matches the sealed structural evidence and identifies the ADR delta.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This assessment persists output. Both /tmp and operation-scratch directory creation were denied by the read-only filesystem, so no assessment was run against the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Could not create the required scratch copy for this persisting assessment. Integration boundaries were reviewed through source, targeted tests and the sealed integration evidence instead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Could not create a scratch copy for this persisting assessment without violating the no-repository-change boundary. No assessment output was written.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only gate; this review requests changes and does not record an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only gate to run after POSE records and verifies the review conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully. Applied the review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose validate --strict; it exited 1 with 235 of 236 checks passing. The evidence ref identifies the historical sealed canonical unit result, which is green; it is not asserted as evidence of a fresh local pass. The local required validation gate remains failed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp; it exited 1. Separately, go test ./internal/cli/ ./internal/pose/ passed the CLI package but timed out in internal/pose after ten minutes. Targeted tests, targeted race tests, build and vet passed. The cited sealed unit result is historical green evidence, not a claim that this independent strict invocation passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
